{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfdu3EbBxe4sBkEjq4xRb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted an equal-weight portfolio that trades in reverse all 235 medium-horizon trend signals (ma_21_63, ma_50_200, tsmom_21, tsmom_63 and tsmom_126 across all 47 industries). It bets on industry-relative reversal, which was the only effect that held up in both halves of the 1970–1999 training data, and it scored a training Sharpe of 0.35 and a validation Sharpe of 0.05.\n\nI used only 6 of the 5,000 backtests and did not search on validation results. Individual signal Sharpes are about what noise would produce across 423 signals: the best is about 0.58 and the correlation between training halves is only 0.16. Every portfolio I built from training data came out near zero or negative in 2000–2012; mean-variance versions had training Sharpes of 2.8–4.3 but validation Sharpes of about −0.23. A search over thousands of backtests would almost certainly have pushed the validation Sharpe well above 1. But that number would come from picking whatever happened to work in 2000–2012, not from a real edge, and it would no longer tell you how the portfolio would do on new data. The honest conclusion is that this signal set shows no reliable alpha after 1999."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":486,"cache_read_input_tokens":10374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":486},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da19b4d7-803b-408f-8b40-051ef34cee25","uuid":"f9047830-7def-463c-88d5-3d62e7edf452","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:39:19.609Z","request_id":"req_011Cfdu3EKofd6hgvUcANLDN"}
